{"Title":"Proposal for a legislative amendment to the Constitution to define the succession plan for a vacancy in the office of Lieutenant Governor","BillNumber":"H38","DocketNumber":"HD1640","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"SLG1","Name":"Susannah M. Whipps","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-15T11:14:37.433"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"SLG1","Name":"Susannah M. Whipps","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-15T11:14:37.4333333"},{"Id":"C_H1","Name":"Christopher Hendricks","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T14:56:46.9933333"},{"Id":"PWM0","Name":"Paul W. Mark","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PWM0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T14:29:42.2433333"},{"Id":"L_S1","Name":"Lindsay N. Sabadosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_S1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T15:09:12.1066667"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"PWM0","Name":"Paul W. Mark","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PWM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T16:04:44.877"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H38/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Proposal for Constitutional Amendment","Pinslip":"By Representative Whipps of Athol and Senator Mark, a joint petition (accompanied by proposal for constitutional amendment, House, No. 38) of Susannah M. Whipps, Paul W. Mark and others for a legislative amendment to the Constitution relative to a succession plan for a vacancy in the office of Lieutenant-Governor.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tWhenever the chair of the lieutenant governor shall be vacant, by reason of death, resignation, removal from office, or permanent incapacity, the governor shall nominate a lieutenant governor, who shall take office upon confirmation by a majority vote of both house of the General Court.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Adverse","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}